@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in/sign-up components, shared document layout and response headers, and the privacy notice. Source audit only; no browser sessions, live credential submissions, or servers were used.
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+- Account payloads already contain only username and password. Kept that contract and added inline purpose, recipient, demo credential guidance, and a link to the privacy notice. No additional identity or consent fields were added.
+- Both account requests now explicitly omit cookies, request no caching, suppress the referrer, and reject redirects. Removed response-body parsing and raw backend error display so tokens and internal error details are not retained or shown. Password state is cleared after completed requests. No client token persistence was introduced.
+- Added POST semantics to prevent the native default GET from placing credentials in a URL before hydration, plus a JavaScript requirement notice. The remote API expects JSON; a functional non-JavaScript submission path would require a server-side integration and remains unavailable.
+- Added stable field names and password-manager autocomplete, disabled text correction for usernames, associated help text, and enforced the existing advertised sign-up password constraint in the browser. Server validation remains the account service's responsibility.
+- Removed the automatically loaded remote analytics script and the commented advertising loader from the shared layout. Ad slot components remain inert without an ad network loader. Removed Google Fonts requests and preconnects, using installed serif fonts instead. Optional tracking is absent by default, so no consent state or cookie banner is needed.
+- Added a document referrer meta policy and actual Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, and X-Content-Type-Options response headers in middleware. Account documents also receive Cache-Control: no-store. Existing features do not require the disabled camera, microphone, location, motion sensors, payment, or USB capabilities.
+- Removed eager reading-list session initialization on every request; the existing reading-list write endpoint initializes its list on the first save.
+- Replaced generic privacy boilerplate and the dead privacy preferences link with a notice and working link reflecting the implementation and known limits.
+
+## Remaining boundaries
+
+The external Google Cloud account service is outside this repository. Verify its password hashing, validation, rate limiting, operational logs, retention/deletion controls, and response cache headers before collecting real personal data. This audit did not make live requests to the account service or verify those controls. The frontend cannot impose retention or deletion on that service.
+
+External editorial images still cause third-party requests. Self-hosting those assets would reduce that exposure further. The plant-stats article retains its intentional cookie/cache demonstration; it is disclosed in the notice and was outside the requested account/layout scope. Session configuration is not present in this repository, so reading-list persistence and session cookie flags need deployment-level review.
+
+A comprehensive script CSP/Trusted Types rollout is deferred: Astro hydration, the client router, and inline article scripts require compatibility work and verification beyond this source-only privacy pass. No telemetry/reporting endpoint was added, avoiding collection of document URLs and script samples.
+
+Validation: `pnpm build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. The build reported existing Vite plugin deprecations and ignored `getStaticPaths` warnings for server-rendered routes. No development/preview server was started and no built server entrypoint was imported.
