 import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
 ---
 <LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news site. You can read articles without creating an account.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="privacy-defaults">Privacy by default and your choices</h2>
+    <p>We do not load optional analytics or advertising scripts. Fonts use your device’s installed fonts, without contacting a font provider. There is no optional tracking to enable or decline in this version of the site.</p>
+
+    <h2>Sign-in and sign-up data</h2>
+    <p>Both forms ask only for a username and password. Your username identifies your demo account; you do not need to provide a real name, email address, phone number, or date of birth. Use made-up credentials and never reuse a password from another service.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, your browser sends those two fields over HTTPS to our account service hosted on Google Cloud at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>. Sign-up requests create a demo account, and sign-in requests check your credentials. As with any network request, the service also receives connection information such as your IP address and browser headers.</p>
+    <p>The forms omit cookies from these requests, request that responses not be cached, and do not send the referring page URL. This frontend does not save your credentials or authentication tokens in local storage or session storage. The password field is cleared after each completed request. Your browser’s password manager may separately offer to save credentials under your control.</p>
+
+    <h2>Retention and account controls</h2>
+    <p>This repository does not contain the account service implementation. Its password storage, logs, retention period, and deletion practices cannot be verified here. This demo currently provides no account export, correction, password recovery, or deletion flow. Avoid submitting personal information; do not use this demo for an account that requires those controls.</p>
+
+    <h2>Other requests and browser storage</h2>
+    <p>Pages and images are requested as you browse. Some editorial images are hosted by external providers, including Imgur and the CinemAI demo service; those providers receive connection information when their images load. The site sends no referring page URL with these requests. Clicking an external link also takes you to a service with its own data practices.</p>
+    <p>The reading-list feature uses a server session when session support is available, which may require a session cookie when you save an article. Ordinary page requests do not initialize a reading list. The “Silent Architects” demo article also contains a cookie-based cache demonstration for its plant-stats endpoint. These are separate from the account forms and are not optional analytics cookies.</p>
+    <p>The hosting and account services may keep operational logs. Their retention settings are outside this frontend repository. Clearing this site’s browser data removes locally stored site data, but does not delete records held by those services.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
